        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-09T07:02:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: no need to make this copy, you can just iterate over the whole set and then clear it once the iteration is finishes. If some other code is modifying this on another thread then this code is incorrect anyway.",
      "revId": "80b8ecfbb7bd5aad0c644094a350027ba6b7e610",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18a9d71e_82c70266",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 10966,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-09T07:02:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per discussion: what if we leave this to a future CL? It\u0027s unlikely that any deployed device actually does this. And I think onUnavailable is actually not the best thing to do here, the most appropriate response would be onLost.\n\nonLost could be sent by either removing the NOT_RESTRICTED capability from the app\u0027s request (but we\u0027ve never done that before once a request was registered) or by changing NetworkAgentInfo#satisfies() method so it checks that app\u0027s permissions instead. This latter path is what Jean and I had in mind when we were talking about changing the semantics of NOT_RESTRICTED to mean \"NOT_RESTRICTED for the particular caller of the requwst / recipient of the callback\".",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10966,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 10966,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "80b8ecfbb7bd5aad0c644094a350027ba6b7e610",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "090a7a09_b6a9b67c",
